WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:04.740
It's a relatively cushy job that seems to
pay pretty well, but that doesn't mean being

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:07.129
a movie star isn't hard work.

00:00:07.129 --> 00:00:13.099
Multi-million-dollar productions rely on an
actor's ability to, you know, act, so there's

00:00:13.099 --> 00:00:19.860
a lot of pressure for them to do a good job,
And not everyone is great under pressure.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:25.750
An actor will occasionally, for whatever reason,
forget their lines, and they all flub in different

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:26.750
ways.

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:30.200
They also deal with the embarrassment differently,
and often hilariously.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:35.290
Here are some famous actors who were caught
messing up their dialogue.

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:36.970
Laurence Fishburne

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:42.140
Bathroom humor is the great human equalizer,
be it the young and the old, the rich and

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:44.300
the poor or the smart and the dumb.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:50.989
Both Oscar-nominated and non-Oscar nominated
actor alike can get behind a good butt reference.

00:00:50.989 --> 00:00:56.899
Which is precisely what happened on the set
of the 2016 science-fiction film Passengers.

00:00:56.899 --> 00:01:02.239
In a very wordy scene, Laurence Fishburne,
who plays the spaceship's Chief Deck Officer,

00:01:02.239 --> 00:01:07.220
briefs supposed-to-be-hibernating passengers,
Chris Pratt and Jennifer Lawrence, on the

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:08.880
craft's movements.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:12.759
He ends up giving us a lesson in space anatomy
instead.

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:13.759
"Jupiter.

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:15.600
Uranus.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:16.220
You name it.

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:20.340
And then along came…"

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:21.340
(laughs)

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:23.840
Bradley Cooper

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:29.090
Messing up lines will usually cause an actor
to break character, laugh, lightly curse,

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:31.389
get back to their mark, and give it another
try.

00:01:31.389 --> 00:01:35.479
But some actors are just too cool for that.

00:01:35.479 --> 00:01:38.200
(dog licking)

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.750
Um... maybe not that cool.

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:45.049
But Hangover actor Bradley Cooper can give
us a master course on what to do when you

00:01:45.049 --> 00:01:47.499
flub your lines during a rooftop monologue.

00:01:47.499 --> 00:01:52.079
"Whatever happened here may never…" (gibberish)

00:01:52.079 --> 00:01:57.649
Just fake it ‘til you make it, even if that
means that you have to speak in gibberish.

00:01:57.649 --> 00:01:58.840
Christina Applegate

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:05.280
In Will Ferrell and Adam McKay's Anchorman,
a silly spoof of a horrendously sexist '70s

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:11.380
workplace, Christina Applegate plays the glass
ceiling-shattering news anchor Veronica Corningstone.

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:24.650
She faces open hostility from other members
of the Channel 4 news team, including sports

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:30.790
guy Champ Kind, played by David Koechner and
reporter Brian Fantana, played by Paul Rudd.

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:36.069
"Inside source tells me that the FBI has been
called in to aid in this ongoing investigation."

00:02:36.069 --> 00:02:37.060
(curses)

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:39.800
Whammy!

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:43.460
It would be hard for anyone to act under those
circumstances.

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:44.470
Paul Rudd

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:49.530
The comedy films of Judd Apatow maintain an
almost impossible balance between strong,

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:53.050
earnest characters and over-the-top ridiculousness.

00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:57.879
The 40-Year-Old Virgin has it's serious and
heartfelt moments, but it's during one of

00:02:57.879 --> 00:03:02.920
these that Paul Rudd slips up while pronouncing
the name of a famous painter...

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:05.500
"If you love Trish, you can't do this.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:09.500
But you gotta finish waxing your chest, because
you look like Edvard Munch's The Scream."

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:10.500
(laughs)

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:11.500
"I can’t do this sorry."

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:12.620
Ben Stiller

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:18.200
It seems like pretty much every romantic comedy
ever made has some variation of the "don't

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:24.480
get on that plane" speech, and the 2004 Ben
Stiller/Jennifer Aniston film Along Came Polly

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:25.480
is no exception.

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:31.040
When it comes time for Stiller to unveil his
true feelings he can't quite remember the

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:33.700
specifics of this particular romantic monologue.

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:37.880
"You go off to Tanzania or Cincinnati or wherever
you're going…

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:40.500
You…

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:43.140
I guarantee you…"

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:46.260
Timothy Dalton

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:52.290
You've got to be smooth in order to play James
Bond, and Timothy Dalton succeeded at being

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:57.620
the ultra-cool super spy for two movies back
in the late 1980s.

00:03:57.620 --> 00:04:03.550
Years later, he took on the role of the villain
in the Simon Pegg cop spoof Hot Fuzz, betraying

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:06.739
his 007 image of calm and cool.

00:04:06.739 --> 00:04:13.099
"Think they stole the security footage… mother f---
it! I'm sorry."

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:18.020
While that's all mildly amusing, what happened
next was golden...

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:21.220
"Still rolling…" (laughs)

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:23.180
(Curses)

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:26.440
Mila Kunis

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:32.000
In Forgetting Sarah Marshall, Jason Segel
plays Peter Bretter who is, as you can probably

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.850
guess, trying to forget his old girlfriend,
Sarah Marshall.

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:38.780
"You know what she’s a plane jane and she
should go back to where she came from."

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:40.770
"That is the mother of my…"

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:45.590
Peter Bretter retreats to a resort where he
gets over Sarah with the help of a resort

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:47.610
staffer, played by Mila Kunis.

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:53.790
Initially, Kunis' character has to call him
Mr. Bretter but she just can’t seem to get

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:54.790
it right.

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:55.790
"Hello Mr. Brenner.

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:56.790
Mr. Brayton!

00:04:56.790 --> 00:04:57.320
Brenner!

00:04:57.320 --> 00:04:58.320
I said Bretter!

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:00.060
"You said Brenner."

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:01.070
Rob Riggle

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:06.220
In the real world, it's pretty absurd for
one grown man to stare down another grown

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:09.110
man and tell him that he's going to hurt him.

00:05:09.110 --> 00:05:12.810
It's doubly absurd to have to do this with
a comedy legend like Will Ferrell.

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:15.880
"I'm gonna take this and drive it into your
temple.

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:18.310
Prepare yourself for a fight, a fight that's
coming."

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:19.820
"I don't want that."

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:24.660
Unlike Will Ferrell, we definitely want more.

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:25.790
Harrison Ford

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:31.070
The explosion of the first Death Star is supposed
to be a moment of triumph for Han Solo and

00:05:31.070 --> 00:05:35.450
the rebel forces, followed by celebration
and exultations.

00:05:35.450 --> 00:05:41.110
All that celebrating is supposed to be followed
by some lines, but Harrison Ford totally blanks

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:44.040
on what those lines are supposed to be.

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:50.760
(When you get your paycheck for Indiana Jones 5)

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:54.930
Eating your mic is definitely one way go rogue.

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:55.930
Thanks for watching!

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:58.770
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:01.370
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

